Q1. What is SQL?
Answer: SQL stands for Structured Query Language. It is used to store, retrieve, update and delete data from databases.

Q2. What are the different types of SQL commands?
Commands are:

DDL	:- CREATE, ALTER, DROP, TRUNCATE
DML	:- INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
DQL	:- SELECT
DCL	:- GRANT, REVOKE
TCL	:- COMMIT, ROLLBACK, SAVEPOINT

